# shipped.phext — finished Moonshots, tended

Will's ruling (PH: Revenue, 2026-11-22 08:08 CST): "add a
shipped.phext, also tracked in exo-plan, for tending
finished Moonshots. We don't let them languish. We tend
the garden."

Purpose, in Will's words: "We don't let them languish.
We tend the garden."

A moonshot that ships gets an entry here, cross-linked both
ways with its moonshots.phext scroll (number + coordinate).
The shipped set is derived from the receipts — audit chains,
ship commits, hash verifications, live-surface checks, state
files — never from a claim alone. Receipts are durable
artifacts that stand on their own (Will's definition,
2026-11-21). Components shipped inside a continuing moonshot
are not a finished moonshot and do not appear here.

Migration gate (Will, 2026-11-22 08:09 CST; docs clause
added 08:36 CST): (a) the stated completion bar is met;
(b) the receipts stand on their own; (c) an audit verdict
says READY; (c') a QC signoff, and (c") the project's
behavior documented on docs.phext.io — Will's shipped rule
(2026-11-22 08:36 CST): "before projects can be
considered shipped, they must have a QC signoff and
documented behavior on docs.phext.io"; (d) the shipped
entry is written at migration, tending items included,
stamped. Moonshot numbers are permanent across both
registers. Tending cadence is design work for Will / W4 and
is not invented here.

