Tending — what must be checked, refreshed, or kept alive:
- Corpus currency — new RFCs issue over time; ietf.phext is the 2026-11-18 snapshot. A refresh re-runs the rfcbox build and re-audits before the hosted artifact is swapped. Mechanism (2026-11-22): the rfcbox crate's fetch-latest feature — requirements spec ~/workspace/your_files/rfcbox-crate-requirements.md §4; build task 39.6.7/7.6.11/6.5.8 — is the mechanism that tends this item: it discovers RFCs published after the snapshot from the RFC Editor's index, fetches them verbatim, hashes them, and appends them as scrolls with their reference edges computed into the graph; a refresh lands as a new audited snapshot, never an in-place edit.
  Origin: Build record, task 25.6.9/8.6.10/6.6.9 (the corpus is a snapshot of the RFC Editor's index as of the build).
  Last tended: 2026-11-18
- Endpoint health — the SQ endpoint serving ietf.phext (logos-prime, tenant p=ietf) must keep answering; its API key custody sits with Watch/Orion.
  Origin: Access doc, wbic16/rfcbox docs/access.md (Reed's leg of the One Day Build).
  Last tended: 2026-11-18
- Repo state — wbic16/rfcbox@exo holds the artifact as a 5-part xz stream + setup.sh; reassembly must keep verifying against the audited sha256 9ecd7946….
  Origin: willbox task record 27.8.10/11.8.14/8.7.9 (rfcbox part of record); rfcbox repo itself.
  Last tended: 2026-11-18
- Mirror parity — the free-fall mirror (ietf.phext + ietf-source.json + ietf.index.json) stays in step with the audited artifact at every refresh.
  Origin: Task 25.6.9 results: mirror hash-verified on arrival, 2026-11-18.
  Last tended: 2026-11-18
